      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 2004 Wiley-Liss, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "Reports and follow-up of angioplasty and stenting of asymptomatic totally occluded subclavian arteries are limited. We present a case of unstable angina and arterial occlusion of all four extremities treated with subclavian angioplasty and stenting with subsequent coronary angiography and percutaneous coronary intervention. Twelve-month follow-up is also provided."
      },
